From: Arvind Yadav <arvind.yadav@intel.com>
Subject: [PATCH v2] drm/xe: Handle purged BOs in VM snapshots

A purged BO can remain in a VM after its TTM resource has been freed.
xe_vm_snapshot_capture() can then dereference a NULL resource while
capturing a devcoredump.

The resource is only stable under the bo reservation, which cannot be
taken here: this runs in the dma_fence_begin_signalling() section opened by
devcoredump_snapshot(), and vm->snap_mutex, held here, is itself taken
under the reservation on the gpuva insert and remove paths.

Read the resource once with READ_ONCE() so the NULL test and the mem_type
access cannot disagree, and record -ENODATA when it is gone. Both consumers
already handle an error pointer: xe_vm_snapshot_capture_delayed() skips
such entries and xe_vm_snapshot_print() reports the error.

This closes the NULL dereference and the TOCTOU. A concurrent free between
the read and the dereference remains possible and would be visible to
KASAN; fixing that requires resolving the region outside the signalling
path, which is left to a follow-up.

Fixes: ad9843aac91a ("drm/xe/madvise: Implement purgeable buffer object support")
Signed-off-by: Arvind Yadav <arvind.yadav@intel.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
index 9e0176861c..c682587453 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
@@ -4513,6 +4513,7 @@ struct xe_vm_snapshot *xe_vm_snapshot_capture(struct xe_vm *vm)
 		struct xe_vma *vma = gpuva_to_vma(gpuva);
 		struct xe_bo *bo = vma->gpuva.gem.obj ?
 			gem_to_xe_bo(vma->gpuva.gem.obj) : NULL;
+		struct ttm_resource *res;
 
 		if (!(gpuva->flags & XE_VMA_DUMPABLE))
 			continue;
@@ -4526,17 +4527,30 @@ struct xe_vm_snapshot *xe_vm_snapshot_capture(struct xe_vm *vm)
 			snap->snap[i].cpu_caching = bo->cpu_caching;
 			snap->snap[i].bo = xe_bo_get(bo);
 			snap->snap[i].bo_ofs = xe_vma_bo_offset(vma);
-			switch (bo->ttm.resource->mem_type) {
-			case XE_PL_SYSTEM:
-			case XE_PL_TT:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 0;
-				break;
-			case XE_PL_VRAM0:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 1;
-				break;
-			case XE_PL_VRAM1:
-				snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 2;
-				break;
+			snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = -1;
+
+			/*
+			 * The resource is only stable under the bo reservation,
+			 * which cannot be taken from the signalling path. Read it
+			 * once so the NULL test and the mem_type access cannot
+			 * disagree; a concurrent free is still possible here.
+			 */
+			res = READ_ONCE(bo->ttm.resource);
+			if (!res) {
+				snap->snap[i].data = ERR_PTR(-ENODATA);
+			} else {
+				switch (res->mem_type) {
+				case XE_PL_SYSTEM:
+				case XE_PL_TT:
+					snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 0;
+					break;
+				case XE_PL_VRAM0:
+					snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 1;
+					break;
+				case XE_PL_VRAM1:
+					snap->snap[i].uapi_mem_region = 2;
+					break;
+				}
 			}
 		} else if (xe_vma_is_userptr(vma)) {
 			struct mm_struct *mm =
